# A THE fixture secret — a test-mode value, committed on purpose.
#
# NFR-31: a committed .env with a real value is a CI-secret-scanner defect;
# a *fixture* with a *test* value is the whole point of the mock-vs-real
# boundary (SECURITY_TEST_PLAN §2 "the signatures are computed against a
# test webhook secret that's committed as a fixture, NOT a real secret").
#
# A real Stripe live/test secret (`whsec_...` you'd get from the Stripe
# dashboard) is NEVER this file. This value exists only so the signature
# is deterministic + reproducible in the dev stack.
{
  "secret": "whsec_test_vercode_dev_stack_secret",
  "note": "test fixture — not a credential; the dev-stack's STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET matches it"
}
